[
\partial_\kappa M_P\le0.
]

## HYPOTHESES

1. Under A($\tau$),
   [
   \partial_\kappa M_P
   ===================

   \Delta_m A'_\kappa C_h(\bar\pi).
   ]
2. $\Delta_m>0$.
3. A($\tau$) maintains $C_h(\bar\pi)\le0$.
4. The card requires $A'_\kappa$ to be bounded but imposes no sign on it.
5. The L2 placebo check requests a nonpositive derivative and records a hump-shaped $M_P$ as a failed A($\tau$)-orientation prediction.

## PROOF

